{"id":"word:hebrew:H6588","type":"word","title":"פֶּשַׁע","subtitle":"H6588 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a revolt (national, moral or religious)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to פֶּשַׁע (H6588) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 93 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"פֶּשַׁע (peshaʻ) means a revolt (national, moral or religious) First listed occurrence: 1Kgs 8 50."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"פֶּשַׁע","transliteration":"peshaʻ","pronunciation":"peh'-shah","strong":"H6588","lemmaId":"hebrew:H6588","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["פִּשְׁעֵ֣י","פָּ֑שַׁע","פִּשְׁעֵי/הֶ֖ם","פִּשְׁעֵי/כֶ֔ם","פִּשְׁעֵי/הֶ֑ם"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",16],["HNcmpc",10],["HR/Ncmsc",7],["HNcmpc/Sp1cs",7],["HNcmpc/Sp3mp",6],["HNcmsc/Sp1cs",6],["HNcmpc/Sp1cp",5],["HNcmpc/Sp2mp",4],["HNcmsc/Sp3mp",4],["HC/Ncmsa",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"a revolt (national, moral or religious)","usage":"rebellion, sin, transgression, trespass.","full":"H6588. pesha מֶּ֫שַׁע noun masculine Psa 19:14 transgression ; — absolute ׳פ Exod 22:8 +, מָּ֑שַׁע Prov 10:9 +; construct מֶּשַׁע Gen 50:17 +; suffix מִּשְׁעִי 31:16 14 t. suffixes; plural מְּשָׁעִים Prov 10:12 ; construct מִּשְׁעֵי Amos 1:3 +, etc.; — 1 transgression against individuals Gen 31:36 ; 50:17 (twice in verse); Exod 22:8 (E), 1Sam 24:12 ; 25:28 ; Prov 10:19 ; 17:19 ; 29:6 , 16 , 22 . ׳פ שְׂפָתַיִם 12:13 ; אַהֲבָה תְּכַסֶה כלפֿשׁעים על 10:12 , compare 17:9 ; 19:11 ; 28:13 . 2 of nation, against nation: Amos 1:3 , 6 , 9 , 11 , 13 ; 2:1 ; of land Prov 28:2 . Elsewhere 3 against God: a. in General, || חטאת Isa 58:1 ; 59:12 ; Micah 1:5 (twice in verse); 1:13 ; 3:8 ; Amos 5:12 ; || עון Ezek 21:29 ; Psa 107:17 ; פ ׳עשׂה Ezek 18:22 , 28 ; פ ׳ביום 33:12 ; פ ׳רַבּוּ Isa 59:12 ; Job 35:6 ; Jer 5:6 (?); פ ׳חטאתו על יֹסִיף Job 34:37 he addeth transgression unto his sin ; פ ׳יִלְדֵי Isa 57:4 ; personified as evil spirit, פשׁע נאם Psa 36:2 . b. as recognized by sinner ; he knows it Psa 51:5 , makes known concerning it to ׳י 32:5 , does not cover it ( כסה ) Job 31:33 ; turns from it Isa 59:20 ; Ezek 18:30 ; casts it away from him 18:31 . c. God deals with it: by visiting it ( פקד ) Amos 3:14 ; Psa 89:33 , dealing with one according to it, כ עשׂה Ezek 39:24 , making it known to sinner Job 13:23 ; 36:9 ; punishing in various ways: ׳מִמּ because of it Isa 53:5 , 8 ; with על , acc . to it Amos 2:4 , 6 ; Lam 1:5 , 22 ; for it, with ב Isa 50:1 ; פ ׳עֹל Lam 1:14 yoke of transgression ; personified, פ בְּיַד ׳וַיְשַׁלְּחֵם Job 8:4 ; be does not grant forgiveness to it, ל נאשׂ ׳לאֹ Exod 23:21 ; Josh 24:19 (E). d. God forgives ( נשׂא ) it Exod 34:7 ; Num 14:18 (J), Job 7:21 , compare Psa 32:1 ; pardons ( סלח ) 1Kin 8:50 ; passes over ( על עבר , compare Prov 19:11 ) Micah 7:18 ; removes ( הרחיק ) Psa 103:12 ; covers over ( כפר ) 65:4 ;-compare (of priest) מִפ עַלהַֿקֹּדֶשׁ ׳וְכִמֶּר Lev 16:16 , and confession of ׳פ over ( על ) goat 16:21 ; &#8212; God blots out ( מחה ) Isa 43:25 ; 44:22 ; Psa 51:3 ; אַלתִּֿזְכֹּר ׳וּפ 25:7 ; delivers from, מן הציל 39:9 . &#8212; Job 35:15 read מֶּשַׁע for פַשׁ q. v. 4 guilt of transgression (compare עון 2 ), פ ׳בְּלִי without (guilt of) transgression Job 33:9 ; 34:6 ; פ ׳לא Psa 59:4 ; ׳פ עלינו Ezek 33:10 ; פ ׳עליה כבד Isa 24:20 ; פ ׳בְּרֹב Psa 5:11 ; מפ ׳נקיתי 19:14 ; יִמַּמְּאוּ : ׳בְּכָלפֿ defile themselves with all (the guilt of) transgressions Ezek 14:11 ; 37:23 ; פ בִּצְרוֺר ׳חָתֻם Job 14:17 . 5 punishment for transgression , Dan 8:12-13 , 9:24 , compare try עון 3 6 offering for transgression , פשׁעי בכורי האתן Micah 6:7 shall I give my first-born as an offering for my trunsgression (compare חטאת 4 ).","rootNote":"from 6586 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Kgs 8 50","keyReferences":["1Kgs 8 50","1Sam 24 12","1Sam 25 28","Amos 1 3","Amos 1 6","Amos 1 9","Amos 1 11","Amos 1 13"],"relate